From f543a98b43be0c84dc3acd5ea8efc8719ff9309e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:10:20 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] hwmon: macsmc: Read die and pressure keys from DT

Use apple,soc-die-keys to append validated die temperature channels after
the existing temperature children. Register the hottest-sensor zone and
pressure attribute from DT data without a machine-compatible gate. Keep
the current validation and failed-read behavior.

All three board table entries now have matching DT data, so remove the
table and the downstream soc_die_keys and board_keys parameters. Neither
parameter is present in the mainline v7.3 driver or its documentation.
Keep the documented fan_control override and DT fan support from the
preceding fan-control series unchanged.

Document the new properties and the requirement to update the DTB with
the kernel when replacing the former board fallback.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
---
 Documentation/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.rst |  18 +++
 drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c         | 160 +++++----------------------
 2 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 132 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.rst b/Documentation/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.rst
index 8aef3dd2bf75..2204745326cb 100644
--- a/Documentation/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.rst
+++ b/Documentation/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.rst
@@ -31,6 +31,20 @@ as unsafe, allows manual speeds on every fan with a mode key whatever the
 Devicetree says. It cannot be proven that the system will fail safe if it
 overheats under a manual fan speed.
 
+SoC die temperatures are described by the ``apple,soc-die-keys`` string list
+on the hwmon device node. The driver appends these temperature channels after
+the ``temperature-*`` children, in list order, with labels ``SoC die <key>``.
+Only readable four-byte floating-point keys are used. When thermal support is
+enabled, their hottest reading supplies the ``macsmc_soc_die`` thermal zone.
+A failed or implausible reading fails the zone read rather than reporting a
+partial result. Keys absent from the firmware are skipped.
+
+The optional ``apple,thermal-pressure-key`` on the same node describes a
+readable signed 32-bit firmware thermal pressure level. Neither feature needs
+a module parameter. Kernels using these properties need an updated device
+tree; the former downstream per-board fallback and its ``soc_die_keys`` and
+``board_keys`` parameters have been removed.
+
 sysfs interface
 ---------------
 
@@ -73,3 +87,7 @@ tempX_input
 tempX_label
     Temperature sensor label
 
+thermal_pressure_level
+    Firmware thermal pressure level, exposed read-only when the device tree
+    supplies a valid key. The integer is firmware-defined and is not a
+    temperature or a percentage.
diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c b/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
